{"author":{"id":"5698b6d16d951325374257d86a2e673da0e55970c3d21c0f7c6f49018f24e5bf"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1786429251,"nonce":"XMyJEbaVUN3VSOKO0XN5yB77DBo=","title":"Soft-deleting a tenant can lock out an unrelated live tenant's user","message":"**What is wrong.** `resolveByEmailSQL` (`internal/identity/repository/users.go:124`) has no `orgs` join, while `resolveSessionSQL` and `resolveByPrefixSQL` both `JOIN orgs o ON … AND o.deleted_at IS NULL`.\n\nTwo consequences:\n\n1. A member of a soft-deleted tenant still passes password verification, and `service.Login` goes on to INSERT a session row for a dead tenant. The handler's later `Me` call refuses (401, no cookie), so nothing is authenticated — but every attempt leaves an orphan `sessions` row that only the expiry sweep removes. Same class as the `TokenPrefixLen` orphans in review-security C2.\n\n2. Worse: the dead org's row still counts toward the `LIMIT 2` that makes `ResolveByEmail` org-blind. A LIVE user in a DIFFERENT org who shares the address becomes 'ambiguous' and cannot log in at all, receiving a 401 that explains nothing. **Soft-deleting a tenant can lock out an unrelated live tenant's user.**\n\n**Why it matters.** This is an availability defect on the authentication path with no diagnostic: the affected user sees the same 401 as a wrong password, and nothing in the logs says 'a deleted org is shadowing this address'. It is also silent — it only appears once two orgs share an address and one is deleted, which is exactly the state a trial-then-churn customer produces.\n\n**Where.** `internal/identity/repository/users.go:124` (`resolveByEmailSQL`); compare `resolveSessionSQL` and `resolveByPrefixSQL` in the same package, which are correct.\n\n**Done when.** `resolveByEmailSQL` excludes soft-deleted orgs the way its two siblings do, no session row is written for a dead tenant, and a live user sharing an address with a deleted tenant's user can log in. Pinned today by `TestResolveByEmailDoesNotExcludeASoftDeletedOrg` in `internal/identity/repository/auth_resolvers_test.go`, which asserts the CURRENT (defective) behaviour and will break loudly when this is fixed.","files":null}]}